WEBVTT

00:03.210 --> 00:04.560
Hi there!

00:04.560 --> 00:07.140
I'm Proppen, the cosplay YouTuber!

00:07.140 --> 00:08.320
Meow!

00:08.320 --> 00:12.780
This time, I'm dressed up as Killer 
Whale-chan from <i>The Sharkborg From Hell 5</i>!

00:12.780 --> 00:15.270
For today's stream, I'll hit up 
Shinjuku in the early morning

00:15.270 --> 00:18.120
and teach the crows to talk!

00:19.170 --> 00:21.390
She always pulls the dumbest stunts.

00:21.390 --> 00:22.830
Doesn't she know it's 3:00 AM?

00:22.830 --> 00:26.290
Huh? Is it me, or is this street fur-reezing?

00:26.610 --> 00:29.420
Hang on, she's right near here.

00:29.420 --> 00:30.680
Oh, there they are!

00:30.680 --> 00:32.070
Crows!

00:32.460 --> 00:35.700
Hey, what are mew all looking at?

00:35.700 --> 00:37.720
Huh? What's that?

00:39.430 --> 00:40.800
No way. What...?

00:40.800 --> 00:41.930
What the heck are <i>those</i>?!

00:41.930 --> 00:43.350
Hands! They're hands!

00:43.350 --> 00:45.390
Meow!

02:20.240 --> 02:21.070
Hey.

02:21.070 --> 02:23.490
You're late, Iwa-san.

02:23.490 --> 02:27.720
My bad. I got called to 
investigation HQ on my way here.

02:28.250 --> 02:31.470
Anyway, I thought I told 
you to secure the scene.

02:31.470 --> 02:35.630
We can't seal a building without the 
owner's permission or a warrant.

02:35.630 --> 02:38.800
And this building's owner is...

02:39.190 --> 02:40.970
<i>Her</i>?

02:41.550 --> 02:45.470
And who told you about this place?

02:46.250 --> 02:47.930
Mister Daren.

02:47.930 --> 02:50.900
Ah. I can trust a referral from him.

02:51.240 --> 02:53.960
Of course, we'd heard about you before that.

02:53.960 --> 02:58.390
Every hitman knows Shinjuku's 
intermediary by reputation.

02:58.390 --> 03:01.700
They say this is a comfy 
place with lax rules.

03:01.700 --> 03:03.420
I'm honored to receive such high praise.

03:03.420 --> 03:07.650
Since you and your sister were Shibuya's aces...

03:07.650 --> 03:10.830
Rinne and Hiiro Horojima.

03:11.550 --> 03:15.340
I don't remember giving out our 
real names, even in Shibuya.

03:15.340 --> 03:16.980
Oh, do forgive me.

03:16.980 --> 03:20.840
I found them so easily that I assumed 
you weren't trying to hide them.

03:21.610 --> 03:23.050
My rules are lax,

03:23.310 --> 03:26.510
but the penalty for breaking 
them should scare you.

03:27.600 --> 03:30.350
Are you kind of a bitch, maybe?

03:30.350 --> 03:32.390
Why, thank you.

03:34.080 --> 03:36.860
Don't talk that way to Clarissa.

03:38.570 --> 03:41.930
You think you're hot stuff 'cause 
you're so big! I hate that!

03:42.740 --> 03:44.030
<i>She's adorable.</i>

03:44.270 --> 03:48.200
In any case, I welcome having 
more people willing to work.

03:48.200 --> 03:52.670
Occult Channel

03:48.200 --> 03:52.670
<b>Apparition in Shinjuku!</b>

03:48.200 --> 03:52.670
<b>What really was the swarm of hands that 
appeared in Shinjuku in the dead of night?!</b>

03:48.630 --> 03:52.670
Especially since I suspect we're 
about to have our hands full.

03:52.670 --> 03:53.370
<b>Occult Channel</b>

03:52.670 --> 03:53.370
<b>Apparition in Shinjuku!</b>

03:52.670 --> 03:53.370
<b>What really was the swarm of hands that appeared in Shinjuku in the dead of night?!</b>

03:53.370 --> 03:54.080
You're sure this photo wasn't edited?

03:53.370 --> 03:54.080
Proppen ran into it during a live stream
 and uploaded a video.

03:53.370 --> 03:54.080
 Proppen's way too lucky, lol.

03:54.790 --> 03:55.540
<b>Apparition in Shinjuku!</b>

03:54.790 --> 03:55.540
<b>What really was the swarm of hands that appeared in Shinjuku in the dead of night?!</b>

03:56.330 --> 03:58.340
Do you have anything to say for yourself?

03:58.990 --> 04:01.070
You see, umm...

04:02.250 --> 04:06.510
Well, you're free to put your peaceful
 life on the back burner if you like...

04:06.510 --> 04:09.850
I guess we'd better come and go 
by the back door for a while.

04:09.290 --> 04:10.560
Here. This is the place.

04:10.250 --> 04:11.850
This is where Solitaire showed up!

04:11.850 --> 04:14.250
...but I don't want attention 
any more than you do.

04:14.250 --> 04:15.780
I'm sorry.

04:15.620 --> 04:18.610
Hands Swarm 
in Late-night Shinjuku?!

04:15.780 --> 04:18.610
Were you controlling all of these hands?

04:18.610 --> 04:20.400
Yes, more or less.

04:20.400 --> 04:24.610
The public can't decide if it was one 
of Solitaire's tricks or a haunting,

04:24.610 --> 04:28.160
but how many people know for 
sure that those things are real?

04:28.160 --> 04:29.450
Good question.

04:29.450 --> 04:32.210
Solitaire and Lemmings probably realized.

04:32.520 --> 04:35.430
As for Xiaoyu-kun, I'm not sure.

04:36.080 --> 04:38.290
His Lordship 


Incoming call

04:38.710 --> 04:41.010
So, what's the plan, Inspector?

04:41.770 --> 04:43.610
Hey, let me through.

04:42.000 --> 04:44.890
For now, how about Arase and I go in again?

04:46.560 --> 04:49.020
You'd better call that 
off right now, Iwa-san.

04:49.810 --> 04:52.350
A headache of a magazine 
reporter just showed up.

04:53.770 --> 04:54.810
So,

04:54.810 --> 04:57.840
a guy who came to have his 
fortune told was Solitaire?

04:57.840 --> 05:03.120
Yes. He had a completely different face, 
but his soul was the same color.

05:03.460 --> 05:05.450
And he had the same ghost haunting him.

05:06.010 --> 05:07.570
What about the high-school girl?

05:07.570 --> 05:08.700
Well...

05:08.700 --> 05:11.090
There, there. There, there.

05:11.090 --> 05:13.000
It's no use, Corpse God-sama.

05:13.000 --> 05:15.300
This girl isn't giving anything away.

05:15.300 --> 05:17.540
But her dog is giving 
 plenty of cuteness!

05:17.540 --> 05:20.270
Huh? There really was a dog?

05:20.270 --> 05:22.720
Yes. It was at her home all along.

05:22.720 --> 05:25.590
But for some reason, she seems 
to have thought it ran away.

05:25.590 --> 05:30.390
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

05:25.900 --> 05:30.390
Her real father was at home, too. 
The one she split up with was an impostor.

05:31.440 --> 05:33.080
One of those sugar daddies?

05:33.080 --> 05:34.040
Sugar daddies?

05:34.040 --> 05:37.750
Daddies 
for
 dessert!

05:34.210 --> 05:35.830
Daddies for dessert!

05:35.830 --> 05:37.770
Sorry. Forget I said anything.

05:38.170 --> 05:40.620
<i>What made Solitaire set 
his sights on this place?</i>

05:41.100 --> 05:45.460
<i>If he asked about that symbol, 
he must've been after us all along.</i>

05:46.320 --> 05:49.490
<i>I guess I'd better let Clarissa know.</i>

05:50.060 --> 05:51.200
So, anyway,

05:51.470 --> 05:55.420
that writing on the wall looks like 
the Fire-Breathing Bug's work to me.

05:55.420 --> 05:59.380
But what are these "Bastard Children 
of Sabaramond" they mentioned?

05:59.850 --> 06:03.260
It made you blow a gasket 
and cast a big, flashy spell.

06:03.770 --> 06:06.300
Does it have to do with your old world?

06:09.230 --> 06:11.580
Arius Sabaramond-san.

06:12.250 --> 06:15.950
He was the head court sorcerer 
of the Byady Empire,

06:15.950 --> 06:19.670
where my teacher and I lived 
a hundred years or more ago.

06:20.230 --> 06:22.190
Now, boy.

06:22.190 --> 06:25.440
I have something to tell 
you before we begin.

06:25.820 --> 06:31.670
Apart from seeing spirits with your Evil 
Eye, you have no aptitude for magic.

06:31.930 --> 06:32.910
<b>SHOCK</b>

06:32.910 --> 06:38.770
Even the Evil Eye is no talent.
 It's essentially a feature of your soul.

06:38.770 --> 06:39.620
<b>SHOOOCK</b>

06:39.620 --> 06:45.170
But rest easy. Talented 
our not, I will raise you.

06:45.650 --> 06:48.860
You'll be the tenth-ranked court sorcerer 
or so when I'm through with you.

06:48.860 --> 06:51.610
<b>SLUMP</b>

06:50.020 --> 06:52.010
Not first, you ask?

06:52.740 --> 06:55.600
You're more ambitious than I took you for.

06:55.600 --> 06:59.810
But the third-ranked, Utsurojuza, 
is a breed apart from those below.

07:01.070 --> 07:02.520
And the second-ranked is me.

07:03.130 --> 07:06.460
Above all, the first-ranked 
is half a politician.

07:06.460 --> 07:08.970
Skill alone won't carry you that far.

07:09.530 --> 07:11.410
I wouldn't say that.

07:12.470 --> 07:16.540
In terms of ability,
 you ought to hold my post.

07:16.540 --> 07:20.500
See, boy? He's already 
come to judge your worth

07:20.500 --> 07:25.460
as a future tool in court politics.

07:26.210 --> 07:28.920
Please, Izliz. Enough snide remarks.

07:29.390 --> 07:33.740
All people are of equal worth. 
I can't assign values to them.

07:36.740 --> 07:42.130
Sabaramond-san was a kind person and 
one of the best-loved in the empire.

07:42.130 --> 07:46.360
People flocked to state 
functions where he appeared.

07:46.810 --> 07:49.320
Sounds like one of our celebrities.

07:49.320 --> 07:51.220
Like Ryouma Kannagi?

07:51.570 --> 07:55.930
I can't believe <i>you</i> named 
an idol and not a shark.

07:55.930 --> 07:57.530
Of course I did.

07:57.530 --> 08:02.030
In his child-actor days, he had a minor 
part in <i>The Sharkborg From Hell Z</i>.

08:00.910 --> 08:09.710
<b>Starring: The Sharkborg 
Costarring: Ryouma Kannagi</b>

08:00.910 --> 08:09.710
<b>Mana Kikimura</b>

08:00.910 --> 08:09.710
<b>Rudy Wong</b>

08:02.030 --> 08:06.140
In the one they're filming now, he returns,
 all grown up, as a semi-protagonist.

08:06.140 --> 08:07.540
Don't you even know that?!

08:07.860 --> 08:09.710
They're making <i>another</i> one?

08:09.710 --> 08:11.960
Well, setting that aside,

08:11.960 --> 08:15.220
how come the Fire-Breathing Bug 
knows about this Sabaramond guy?

08:15.220 --> 08:17.410
I'd like to know that, too.

08:17.410 --> 08:21.680
It sounded like they oppose a group called 
the "Bastard Children of Sabaramond."

08:21.680 --> 08:25.900
But that guy was from a hundred 
years ago. Isn't he dead by now?

08:25.900 --> 08:30.290
I don't know what happened to 
Sabaramond-san after the empire fell,

08:30.290 --> 08:35.610
but a sorcerer of his level would be 
able to extend his life a century or two.

08:35.610 --> 08:38.200
Your world's magic is something else.

08:38.200 --> 08:42.660
Skilled sorcerers can delay aging, you see.

08:42.660 --> 08:46.300
But that's not the important part, right?

08:46.300 --> 08:49.060
If this guy is involved,

08:49.060 --> 08:52.450
wouldn't that make his 
"children" your allies?

08:52.450 --> 08:53.840
<i>Well...</i>

08:54.850 --> 08:57.480
<i>I don't want my memories of him to be defiled.</i>

08:58.020 --> 08:59.320
<i>But what if</i>

09:00.100 --> 09:05.100
<i>the "Bastard Children of Sabaramond" 
really are part of the empire?</i>

09:05.920 --> 09:10.730
<i>I ran away from that world and into 
this one purely for my own sake.</i>

09:11.510 --> 09:14.950
<i>I'd be the real outsider to all this.</i>

09:15.480 --> 09:16.580
<i>Even so...</i>

09:17.590 --> 09:19.160
<b>STARE</b>

09:21.370 --> 09:22.780
I understand.

09:23.540 --> 09:28.160
Yes, perfectly. Just like 
with Hosorogi five years ago.

09:29.500 --> 09:32.390
Everything is under Sabaramond's aegis.

09:33.290 --> 09:36.740
The previous snipers have left this district,

09:37.370 --> 09:41.410
but one of the Agakuras just 
happens to have an opening.

09:42.920 --> 09:43.810
Listen up.

09:43.950 --> 09:47.690
<b>Authorized personnel only
Underground water tank
 to be built on this site</b>

09:44.080 --> 09:47.690
Our job is to be a diversion, 
so make your kills flashy!

09:48.260 --> 09:51.940
We're not people; we're bullets in flight.

09:51.940 --> 09:55.230
Resist desire and rage dispassionately.

09:55.230 --> 09:58.700
Prove that we're a match for the 
Heilei and the Agakuras at—

10:00.080 --> 10:00.880
What?

10:01.770 --> 10:04.370
How is he so huge?!

10:12.000 --> 10:13.590
What a shame.

10:13.810 --> 10:15.690
A crying shame.

10:15.690 --> 10:19.790
You were so close. Just off by a hair.

10:19.790 --> 10:24.580
You failed to become "bullets in flight" 
just before you would've really soared.

10:25.200 --> 10:26.950
You see, bullets

10:26.950 --> 10:29.180
shouldn't get scared.

10:29.580 --> 10:33.970
You didn't prove you could measure 
up to us Agakuras at all.

10:36.190 --> 10:38.570
<i>How's it going, Momoya?</i>

10:39.130 --> 10:40.670
All done.

10:40.670 --> 10:44.580
That was a close one. I almost died.

10:44.960 --> 10:48.950
I don't know who these guys are, 
but I bet they were crazy tough.

10:48.950 --> 10:50.540
Are you all okay, Nee-san?

10:51.030 --> 10:53.850
You took on their main force, right?

10:53.850 --> 10:55.050
How many of you died?

10:55.050 --> 10:57.690
<i>Not a scratch on us. 
It was over in five seconds.</i>

10:57.690 --> 10:59.020
I'm sorry to hear that.

10:59.020 --> 11:02.300
<i>While you're feeling sorry, 
have a new job, Momoya.</i>

11:02.530 --> 11:07.900
<i>Visit the Shibuya intermediary. 
They've got work for you in Shinjuku.</i>

11:08.670 --> 11:10.970
Shinjuku? Well now.

11:10.970 --> 11:14.060
I'd like Solitaire's autograph 
if I run into him.

11:19.380 --> 11:20.100
Yes.

11:21.370 --> 11:23.920
What on earth was that, Your Lordship?!

11:23.920 --> 11:26.250
<i>Easy, Xiaoyu. Keep calm.</i>

11:26.250 --> 11:30.230
I know something I couldn't see 
stopped Lemmings and Solitaire.

11:30.230 --> 11:32.710
I suspected a stealth suit or something,

11:32.710 --> 11:34.710
<b>A Ghostly Happening
 or One of
 Solitaire's Tricks?!</b>

11:32.710 --> 11:34.710
<i>but that was no trick!</i>

11:34.710 --> 11:37.550
<i>Something really was there!</i>

11:37.550 --> 11:39.020
<i>The fake Polka...</i>

11:39.020 --> 11:42.040
<i>I knew I should have eliminated him!</i>

11:42.040 --> 11:43.550
Just listen.

11:44.020 --> 11:47.470
Whatever it was didn't attack you, did it?

11:47.470 --> 11:51.180
Doesn't that mean it was on your side?

11:52.490 --> 11:53.890
Do you know something?

11:54.480 --> 11:58.610
Xiaoyu, what was the job I asked you to do?

12:00.340 --> 12:04.330
To guard Miss Sayo and the fake Polka... sir.

12:04.330 --> 12:06.530
<i>Just make sure you don't forget that.</i>

12:07.280 --> 12:08.990
Forgive me.

12:09.400 --> 12:12.730
I do know the fake Polka's secret,

12:12.730 --> 12:17.540
but you couldn't believe or accept 
anything I told you now, could you?

12:18.130 --> 12:19.650
O-Of course I could!

12:19.650 --> 12:23.380
<i>You don't believe me when I say 
the fake Polka's all right.</i>

12:23.740 --> 12:25.260
But that's...

12:25.260 --> 12:29.960
Well, words can't do it justice in any case.

12:30.530 --> 12:31.100
I know.

12:31.540 --> 12:34.840
Ask that fellow with Polka's face yourself.

12:34.840 --> 12:38.190
If he refuses to tell you, 
I'll beg him to reconsider.

12:38.190 --> 12:42.500
N-No! Your Lordship should 
never beg someone like him!

12:42.500 --> 12:45.530
<i>Then work hard to earn his trust.</i>

12:45.530 --> 12:48.490
I put my trust in that fake Polka.

12:49.030 --> 12:52.340
<i>So try to open up a little and talk to him.</i>

12:57.840 --> 12:58.970
What is it?

12:59.360 --> 13:03.840
Shinjuku is Kuraki's territory, 
so I'd prefer to avoid standing out.

13:03.840 --> 13:07.570
Oh, I just spotted a familiar face.

13:07.570 --> 13:13.060
He looks great for someone who had his 
arms and legs torn off. I respect that.

13:13.380 --> 13:16.770
They're as tough as centipedes, you know...

13:17.450 --> 13:20.270
those Heilei guys.

13:21.420 --> 13:22.960
What's up, Arase?

13:23.450 --> 13:24.570
Nothing.

13:24.570 --> 13:27.720
I just thought I saw a familiar face.

13:28.500 --> 13:30.640
<i>But there's no way, right?</i>

13:32.690 --> 13:34.790
So, what are you gonna do, Polka?

13:34.790 --> 13:38.250
Anything to do with the other 
world is basically your call.

13:38.890 --> 13:40.060
I...

13:40.710 --> 13:42.380
Morning!

13:43.160 --> 13:44.840
G-Good morning.

13:45.550 --> 13:46.630
What's up?

13:46.870 --> 13:49.760
You're all gloomy! You can't 
go around looking like that!

13:49.760 --> 13:50.970
C'mon, smile!

13:52.910 --> 13:53.720
What the—?!

13:53.720 --> 13:55.330
Pleased to meet you!

13:55.330 --> 13:58.270
Here's my card.

13:56.410 --> 13:58.250
<b></b>Weekly Dry

13:56.410 --> 13:58.250
<b></b>Editorial Department

13:56.410 --> 13:58.250
<b></b>Kochou Eightport

13:59.720 --> 14:01.570
<i>Weekly Dry</i>?

14:01.570 --> 14:05.280
Yup! She says we're gonna be in the news!

14:06.010 --> 14:06.960
Huh?

14:10.010 --> 14:18.000
<i></i>Weekly Dry<i>, a tabloid launched by the 
publishing arm of Anywhere, Inc. in 1996.</i>

14:18.000 --> 14:20.350
<b>...appropriate financing... 
 Bank clerk faced with...</b>

14:18.000 --> 14:25.570
<b><i>Big Scoop</i></b>

14:18.000 --> 14:28.970
<b>Forbidden love Two Nights a Week! 
On-Street Kiss of Betrayal 
Secret Talks and Embraces on Film Fly in the Face of Public Appearances</b>

14:18.290 --> 14:20.450
<i>It covers everything from 
straitlaced politics</i>

14:19.600 --> 14:28.970
<b>Cryptid News Bulletin 
Presenting the First Color Photos of the Abominable Snowman! 
 Man Abducted by Snowman Breaks Silence</b>

14:20.450 --> 14:24.720
<i>to the arts, gossip, the occult, 
and even the latest video games.</i>

14:24.720 --> 14:28.970
<i>And moving 220,000 copies a week makes 
it one of the biggest domestic magazines.</i>

14:28.970 --> 14:32.180
<i>But the Corpse God has 
no way of knowing that!</i>

14:32.460 --> 14:34.390
<i>Not even the real Polka has a clue!</i>

14:34.680 --> 14:38.250
<i>Kochou Eightport is 
</i>Weekly Dry<i>'s best cub reporter!</i>

14:38.250 --> 14:44.400
<i>A fearless investigator who's landed many 
scoops in politics and entertainment!</i>

14:44.860 --> 14:51.320
<i>Can Polka and friends defend their peace 
from the media's sudden onslaught?!</i>

14:51.550 --> 14:53.910
<i>Fight on, Takumi! Don't give in, Takumi!</i>

14:53.910 --> 14:56.290
<i>You're our only hope!</i>

14:56.540 --> 14:58.010
<i>...only hope!</i>

14:57.810 --> 15:00.250
<b>Self-narrating to escape reality</b>

14:58.010 --> 14:58.860
<i>...hope!</i>

14:58.860 --> 14:59.660
<i>...ope!</i>

15:00.250 --> 15:01.960
I-In the news?

15:01.960 --> 15:05.550
Yup! It'll be our national debut!

15:05.950 --> 15:09.800
Umm... I haven't done anything. I'm innocent.

15:09.800 --> 15:12.250
<i>Spoken like a guilty person!</i>

15:12.250 --> 15:15.470
<i>Spoken like someone who gets eaten 
by a shark midway through the movie.</i>

15:16.570 --> 15:19.030
Please, don't be so nervous.

15:19.030 --> 15:23.440
I'm only here to interview the new 
fortune teller everyone's talking about!

15:23.680 --> 15:26.020
Oh, the fortune tell—

15:26.250 --> 15:30.780
Sorry, but we can't trust a reporter 
who snaps photos without asking.

15:30.780 --> 15:32.280
Sorry about that.

15:32.280 --> 15:34.770
I wanted to get you looking natural.

15:35.170 --> 15:38.500
You're free to refuse the 
interview, of course.

15:38.770 --> 15:42.100
Although, in that case, 
I'll report on a different story.

15:42.100 --> 15:43.710
Like what?

15:43.710 --> 15:48.050
Like the mystery of the drones 
that sometimes fly in this area.

15:48.050 --> 15:52.680
It would be awful if some info broker 
was filming people without permission.

15:52.680 --> 15:57.390
<i>Damn her! She looked me up ahead of time!</i>

15:57.630 --> 15:59.850
<i>Oh, now I get it.</i>

16:00.090 --> 16:05.580
<i>She's out to expose a fraud who works 
with an info broker to fake fortunes.</i>

16:03.040 --> 16:05.580
<b>Breaking News 
Dark Collusion Between Ex-Gangster 
Information Broker 
and Fortune-Telling Fraud Exposed!</b>

16:05.580 --> 16:06.940
<b>OOOH HO HO HO HO HO</b>

16:05.580 --> 16:06.940
<b>OOOH HO HO HO HO HO</b>

16:07.230 --> 16:10.120
<i>It won't be a huge deal 
if she thinks we're fakes.</i>

16:10.120 --> 16:13.570
<i>The problem is what happens when 
suspicion shifts to Clarissa.</i>

16:13.820 --> 16:16.110
<i>Once that happens,</i>

16:16.960 --> 16:18.730
<i>"bad news" won't even begin to cover it.</i>

16:19.700 --> 16:22.290
<i>I need to smooth things over somehow.</i>

16:22.920 --> 16:27.860
<i>Takumi Kuruya, former information 
specialist for the Sanzu Sons gang.</i>

16:28.420 --> 16:32.740
<i>Once a boy genius, you launched 
a software company at age fourteen</i>

16:33.170 --> 16:36.970
<i>but unscrupulous adults took over the business</i>

16:37.520 --> 16:39.160
<i>and drove your family to suicide.</i>

16:39.610 --> 16:43.420
<i>As the sole survivor, you entered 
the criminal underworld.</i>

16:44.410 --> 16:47.350
<i>Your life would make a good article,</i>

16:47.350 --> 16:49.630
<i>but you're not my target now.</i>

16:53.310 --> 16:54.890
A fortune teller?

16:54.890 --> 17:00.220
Yes. I want to interview Shinjuku's 
newest fortune teller, "the Corpse God."

17:00.220 --> 17:03.120
Would you spare me the 
page real estate for it?

17:03.120 --> 17:08.900
I don't see why not, but weren't 
you working on the Solitaire case?

17:08.900 --> 17:10.730
Yes, Solitaire!

17:10.730 --> 17:13.590
But this interview is connected.

17:13.590 --> 17:14.440
Huh?

17:14.440 --> 17:20.510
You see, detectives on the Solitaire 
case visited this fortune teller

17:20.510 --> 17:25.520
right after investigating the fake "Bug" 
who set fire to the Shinoyama place.

17:26.040 --> 17:30.560
And I've heard that the fortune 
teller may be a Shinoyama himself.

17:30.560 --> 17:33.330
Really? Still, that's not much to go on.

17:33.330 --> 17:37.060
I know that those detectives 
never waste their time.

17:37.390 --> 17:40.650
And my veteran reporter's 
instinct is telling me

17:40.980 --> 17:43.940
that Solitaire's escape, the Shinoyama fire,

17:43.940 --> 17:47.690
and the mysterious fortune 
teller are all connected.

17:47.690 --> 17:52.300
I could even find out if the police 
really tried to shoot Solitaire!

17:52.640 --> 17:55.760
Wait, your <i>veteran's</i> instinct?

17:53.860 --> 17:55.760
<b>It's only 
your third 
year...</b>

17:56.020 --> 17:59.220
Well, as long as you'll 
stick to fortune-telling...

18:00.430 --> 18:02.770
Thank you so much!

18:02.770 --> 18:05.640
I hope we'll have a great 
working relationship!

18:06.070 --> 18:09.110
So, should I start by telling your fortune?

18:09.110 --> 18:13.140
No, I'd like to make this 
as objective as possible.

18:13.140 --> 18:18.820
So, if you don't mind, I'll provide 
a customer tomorrow or later.

18:18.820 --> 18:21.020
Is that so? All right.

18:21.020 --> 18:24.900
Don't interview people waiting in line, okay?

18:24.900 --> 18:28.040
Some of them have reasons 
for wanting privacy.

18:28.040 --> 18:31.020
Of course. I won't cause any trouble!

18:31.020 --> 18:32.810
What a nice reporter!

18:33.200 --> 18:34.730
I sure hope so.

18:34.730 --> 18:36.690
Now, let's get ready to open shop.

18:36.690 --> 18:37.970
Me, too!

18:39.030 --> 18:40.460
<i>Talk about bingo!</i>

18:40.460 --> 18:42.680
<i>This is the mother of all jackpots!</i>

18:43.120 --> 18:46.800
<i>I can't believe Solitaire 
visited here this morning too!</i>

18:46.800 --> 18:50.690
<i>And if my sources are accurate, 
the Corpse God's real name</i>

18:50.690 --> 18:52.620
<i>is Polka Shinoyama.</i>

18:52.620 --> 18:56.950
<i>It makes no sense for a Shinoyama to be 
telling fortunes with an info broker,</i>

18:56.950 --> 19:00.370
<i>but he looked relieved to hear 
that's what I'm reporting on!</i>

19:00.370 --> 19:02.410
<i>I knew he was fishy.</i>

19:02.750 --> 19:03.660
<i>And...</i>

19:04.320 --> 19:07.510
<i>isn't that what the Fire-Breathing 
Bug leaves at crime scenes?!</i>

19:07.840 --> 19:10.620
<i>I'm drawing so many winning 
tickets, it scares me!</i>

19:10.620 --> 19:13.330
<i>But as a reporter, I have to ask!</i>

19:10.620 --> 19:13.330
<b><b>TWITCH
 TWITCH 
TWITCH 
TWITCH</b></b>

19:13.330 --> 19:14.540
Umm...

19:14.540 --> 19:17.290
I've been wondering about 
that writing on the wall.

19:17.290 --> 19:19.720
Do you support the Fire-Breathing Bug?

19:19.720 --> 19:21.380
Huh? When did that—

19:21.840 --> 19:24.990
Nothing to see here. 
Just our daily shark-wrestling.

19:25.610 --> 19:28.920
This graffiti's been here 
since before we moved in.

19:28.920 --> 19:31.770
We just can't be bothered to get 
rid of it. Does it mean something?

19:31.770 --> 19:34.520
Y-Yes! That's right!

19:34.520 --> 19:36.610
<i>Just stop talking!</i>

19:36.980 --> 19:38.400
Is that so?

19:38.910 --> 19:40.320
<i>Suspicious.</i>

19:40.580 --> 19:43.490
<i>The writing looks brand-new,</i>

19:43.490 --> 19:47.040
<i>but maybe assuming the Bug's involvement 
was jumping to conclusions.</i>

19:47.570 --> 19:49.450
<i>No, I can't let my guard down.</i>

19:49.450 --> 19:51.920
<b>Shinoyama Group... 

Culprit's...</b>

19:49.450 --> 19:54.800
<i>The Shinoyama Group has more than 
its fair share of shady rumors, too.</i>

19:56.810 --> 19:59.590
So, you weren't hurt, Nezu?

20:01.890 --> 20:03.130
I see.

20:03.130 --> 20:04.970
Then let's review.

20:05.380 --> 20:08.220
That wasn't one of 
Solitaire's tricks, was it?

20:10.060 --> 20:11.030
Very well.

20:12.860 --> 20:14.820
Take a little time off.

20:15.140 --> 20:18.920
Both Solitaire and my grandfather's 
bodyguard will be on the lookout for you.

20:19.320 --> 20:21.030
And, starting next week,

20:21.250 --> 20:23.380
your main job should keep you busy.

20:26.430 --> 20:29.600
No need to thank me. 
Just stay healthy and fit.

20:31.170 --> 20:33.870
<i>That pause was a thank you?</i>

20:35.590 --> 20:36.550
Taipei.

20:37.220 --> 20:38.040
Sir.

20:38.040 --> 20:41.760
Coordinate with the Lei main 
force to pursue Solitaire.

20:42.000 --> 20:45.190
Operate near the building 
where Polka is yourself.

20:45.600 --> 20:46.720
May I kill him?

20:46.720 --> 20:52.180
Prioritize taking him alive.
 I'm curious what he knows about Polka.

20:52.720 --> 20:56.150
And I'd like to thank him for 
hurting our company's share prices.

20:56.910 --> 20:57.980
As you wish.

20:58.410 --> 20:59.100
Bao.

20:59.450 --> 21:00.190
Mmm.

21:00.400 --> 21:02.610
Provide informational support.

21:03.160 --> 21:05.150
Mmm. Got it.

21:05.150 --> 21:08.860
The police have assigned numerous 
personnel to Solitaire, as well.

21:08.860 --> 21:10.910
I'm already having them monitored,

21:10.910 --> 21:13.700
but they're likely aware of our movements.

21:14.370 --> 21:18.880
Don't underestimate the police force.
 It's truly a lair of demons.

21:19.840 --> 21:23.300
Takeru Shinoyama

21:20.480 --> 21:23.300
I wondered who was snooping around.

21:23.600 --> 21:25.430
The Shinoyamas, is it?

21:26.230 --> 21:27.760
Depending on the circumstances,

21:27.760 --> 21:31.180
I may need to ask them 
all to leave the stage.

21:32.240 --> 21:36.520
Yes, I think they're linked in more 
interesting ways than I'd imagined!

21:36.520 --> 21:38.140
<i>Are you sure?</i>

21:38.140 --> 21:41.620
<i>I mean, we'll at least get an 
occult piece out of it, but...</i>

21:41.620 --> 21:43.990
Leave it to me, Chief!

21:44.530 --> 21:47.200
My instincts are telling me

21:47.200 --> 21:52.660
that interesting things are going 
to keep happening in this building!

21:54.870 --> 21:57.120
Oh, you know,

21:57.120 --> 21:58.970
since he's a bartender,

21:58.970 --> 22:03.950
I should've taken inspiration from 
a cocktail when I killed him.
